<title>INDIA: Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 10.16 pct.</title>
<headline>Yield on Indian 91-day t-bill rises to 10.16 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off of 97.53 rupees at the weekly auction of 91-day treasury bills on Friday, down from 97.56 at the previous auction.</p>
<p>Dealers said the yield worked out to 10.16 percent, up from 10.03 percent.  </p>
<p>.</p>
